# Command treemd

## What does this command do:

A (TUI/CLI) Markdown navigator with tree-based structural navigation.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/Epistates/treemd/releases/download/v0.10.0/treemd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xzO treemd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu > ~/.local/bin/treemd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/treemd`
For Raspberry Pi install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/Epistates/treemd/releases/download/v0.10.0/treemd-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xzO treemd-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu > ~/.local/bin/treemd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/treemd`
For Mac install using: `brew install treemd`
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/Epistates/treemd/releases/download/v0.10.0/treemd-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xzO treemd-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu > ~/.local/bin/treemd && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/treemd`

> Note: the Mac container runs Fedora Linux on ARM (aarch64), not x86_64. When a
> package is not installed via `dnf`, download the `aarch64`/`arm64` build of the
> binary — never the `x86_64`/`amd64` build used on the Fedora workstation.
> The container's `~/.local` is wiped on rebuild, so reinstall after a rebuild.

The archive member is named after the build (for example
`treemd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`), not `treemd`, so it must be renamed on install.

## Command path

For Fedora run: `~/.local/bin/treemd`
For Raspberry Pi run: `~/.local/bin/treemd`
For Mac run: `/opt/homebrew/bin/treemd`
For Mac container run: `~/.local/bin/treemd`

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/Epistates/treemd

## Command options

# Open a file in the TUI
treemd README.md

# Pick a file in a directory
treemd .

# Open a URL, or a GitHub repository's README
treemd https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/HEAD/README.md
treemd github:epistates/treemd

# Read from stdin
cat doc.md | treemd -l

# List headings, with their line ranges
treemd -l README.md
treemd -l -n README.md

# Show the heading tree
treemd --tree README.md

# Narrow a listing by text or by level (1-6)
treemd -l --filter install README.md
treemd -l -L 2 README.md

# Heading list as JSON (--output: plain, json, tree)
treemd -l -o json README.md

# Print one section
treemd -s Installation README.md

# Find the heading at or before a line number
treemd --at-line 42 README.md

# Count headings by level
treemd --count README.md

# Query the document (full syntax: treemd --query-help)
treemd -q '.h2' README.md
treemd -q '.code[rust]' README.md
treemd -q '.h1[Features] > .h2' README.md
treemd -q '.link | url' README.md

# Query output format: plain, json, json-pretty, jsonl, md, tree
treemd -q '.h2' --query-output json README.md

# Exit 1 when a query matches nothing
treemd -q '.h2[Install]' -e README.md || echo "no install section"

# Theme, color mode and images in the TUI
treemd --theme Nord README.md
treemd --color-mode 256 README.md
treemd --no-images README.md
treemd --images README.md

# Shell completions (interactive; edits your shell config)
treemd --setup-completions

# Man page
treemd --man-page > treemd.1

# Version / help
treemd --version
treemd --help

# Key bindings (in the TUI)
#   j/k or arrows  next/previous heading     g/G      first/last heading
#   p              parent heading            Tab      switch pane
#   d/u            page down/up              w        hide the outline
#   Enter          fold in the outline       m / '    set / jump to bookmark
#   /              search the section        s        filter the outline
#   f              follow a link by number   i        step through elements
#   e              open editor at the line   y        copy the element
#   :              command palette           ?        list all keys
#   Ctrl+z         undo the last edit
#
# Table cell edits are written straight back to the file.
